WEBVTT

00:00:04.156 --> 00:00:05.470
OT topologies connect physical processes with control, supervision, engineering,

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:06.620
operations, and enterprise functions.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:07.590
At the field level,

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:11.840
sensors measure process conditions and actuators create physical action.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.500
Controllers such as PLCs and RTUs read inputs, execute logic, and update outputs.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.485
Human-machine interfaces give operators visibility into status, alarms, trends,

00:00:20.485 --> 00:00:21.391
and commands.

00:00:21.391 --> 00:00:26.389
SCADA systems coordinate monitoring and supervisory control across distributed assets.

00:00:26.389 --> 00:00:30.730
Distributed control systems support coordinated control within plants or processes.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.120
Engineering workstations configure controllers and applications,

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.840
while historians store time-series operational data.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:40.285
These systems also connect to site services and enterprise applications for scheduling,

00:00:40.285 --> 00:00:43.500
reporting, maintenance, identity, remote support, and analytics.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.680
Purdue-style layers can provide a useful mental model for these functions,

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:50.550
but the actual environment may include cloud platforms, wireless devices,

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:55.152
vendor appliances, remote sites, and legacy links that cross traditional boundaries.

00:00:55.152 --> 00:00:57.548
Topology matters because communication paths shape risk.

00:00:57.548 --> 00:01:01.920
A reporting flow from a historian to an enterprise application has different consequences

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.755
from an engineering path that can modify controller logic.

00:01:04.755 --> 00:01:09.235
A remote support connection may bypass expected boundaries if it uses a separate cellular

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.800
or vendor-managed service.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:14.840
Accurate diagrams should show assets, trust boundaries, data and control flows,

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:18.295
remote access, dependencies, redundancy, and external connections.

00:01:18.295 --> 00:01:22.530
This information supports segmentation, monitoring placement, vulnerability analysis,

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.136
and incident containment.

00:01:24.136 --> 00:01:24.845
During response,

00:01:24.845 --> 00:01:28.395
teams need to know which functions can continue locally and what may be lost when a

00:01:28.395 --> 00:01:29.366
connection is isolated.

00:01:29.366 --> 00:01:33.390
Security architecture begins with understanding how the operation actually communicates.
